e it's taken me a long time to  figure out what to have for breakfast  that didn't leave me feeling bloated  didn't feel me leaving uncomfortable  throughout the rest of the day and a  chia seed breakfast bowl has been the  best thing that i've had as i'm coming  to the end of breakfast that's usually  when i look at my stats from the night  before i look at the quality of my sleep  the quality of my rem sleep my deep  sleep i look at what i need to do today  and what i love about the auraing app is  that it guides me and coaches me  throughout my day it will tell me what  time i should aim to be asleep it will  tell me what to avoid it will even tell  me to stay active for me it's really  useful having this guide in my pocket  and helping me make my choices  throughout the day and then i sit down  for my favorite cup of herbal tea  usually it's a fresh mint and for me  having a warm cup of herbal tea allows  me to again start grounded i love the  scent  i love the feeling of the warmth inside  of my body and i love the cleansing  effect that it has and so this is where  i am now all of these habits have had a  huge impact on my life and that's why  i'm sharing them with you and habit  number 10 the last one before some very  special bonus clips is set a timeline  with alex ortner what are some  fundamental must-haves you feel like  for that evening wind down or or evening  routine  um  i mean for me for starters uh it is  actually setting timelines on the things  and the way you shut yourself down or  slow yourself down from the day and i've  got the same structure for my kids and  then a lot of myself evolves around my  kids so i know that for my kids now it's  eight o'clock all devices are off and  that includes adults um all of us  devices are off at eight o'clock eight  o'clock to nine o'clock it's that  getting ready for bed it's spending time  together it's like calming our body down  so that we can get ready for bed right  and just being present with each ot